<item><title>Egypt and Kuwait sign agreements at joint committee</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-and-kuwait-sign-agreements-at-joint-committee-6fff6d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-and-kuwait-sign-agreements-at-joint-committee-6fff6d/</guid><category>Egypt</category><description>The 14th session of the Egyptian-Kuwaiti Joint Committee ended with several agreements and memoranda of understanding signed in Kuwait on Sunday.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:41:40 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/eg.jpg" length="31241" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/eg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Egypt starts service of first two Alstom trains on Cairo Metro Line 1</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-starts-service-of-first-two-alstom-trains-on-cairo-252797/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-starts-service-of-first-two-alstom-trains-on-cairo-252797/</guid><category>Egypt</category><description>The French-built trains are the first deliveries under a contract to supply 55 trains for the country&apos;s oldest metro line.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:46:33 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/eg.jpg" length="31241" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/eg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Spotted hyena returns to Egypt&apos;s Red Sea Governorate</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/spotted-hyena-returns-to-egypt-s-red-sea-governorate-27fed9/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/spotted-hyena-returns-to-egypt-s-red-sea-governorate-27fed9/</guid><category>Egypt</category><description>Villagers in Abu Ramad found mutilated sheep, signaling the return of a predator unseen for over five millennia.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:45:46 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/eg.jpg" length="31241" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/eg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Egypt captured most of Europe&apos;s fertilizer market as its gas kept flowing</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-captured-most-of-europe-s-fertilizer-market-as-its-2d5d77/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-captured-most-of-europe-s-fertilizer-market-as-its-2d5d77/</guid><category>Egypt</category><description>Egyptian factories supplied more than 60 percent of the fertilizer that reached European markets during the March to September season.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:44:34 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-captured-most-of-europe-s-fertilizer-market-as-its-2d5d77/share.jpg" length="45344" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-captured-most-of-europe-s-fertilizer-market-as-its-2d5d77/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
